  {
    "topper": "Timing",
    "title": "How Often, and When to Trim",
    "image": "ladder-oak",
    "html": "<p>South Florida trees grow nearly all year, so there is no single off-season. A practical calendar:</p><ul><li><strong>Late winter to spring:</strong> assess and prune structure before the growing season and before hurricane season.</li><li><strong>June to November:</strong> hurricane season. Remove dead and hazardous limbs; avoid heavy cutting that stresses trees in the heat.</li><li><strong>After any storm:</strong> remove broken limbs and hangers, and have damaged trees checked.</li><li><strong>All year:</strong> palms, whenever dead fronds hang over a roof, pool or walkway.</li></ul><p>Fast-growing species such as ficus and black olive often need attention every year or two.</p>"
